            <div xml:id="d729">

                <pb facs="0781" n="467" xml:id="pg467"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1266a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1911-11-27T21:13:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 27, 1911, 9:13 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>628. Press reports state that British Government has mined the River Tyne and the
                    Firth of Forth. Please investigate and report to Department. An early reply is
                    requested.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
